# Allow-list: ignore EVERYTHING, then re-include only what the image needs.
# Safer than a deny-list, because a new file (a .env, a key, a 2 GB dataset)
# is excluded by default instead of leaking into the build context and image.
#
# Example: `docker build .` now sends only a few KB to the daemon, not .venv/ (~60 MB) or .git/.
*
!app/
!requirements.lock

# Even inside app/, skip bytecode caches.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
